    "long_instructions": "# Modify: Add the Else\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter is painting the street, but it starts with no paint. At every square it reaches, it checks whether it's standing on the bucket. If it is, it restocks. If it isn't, it should paint. Right now the Painter walks along and never paints anything. Fix the program.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Run the program and watch the Painter. Does it paint anything? Which parts of the code ran?\r\n2. Add an `else` branch to each `if` so the Painter paints the square it's standing on when it isn't on the bucket.\r\n3. Run your program again. Which branch ran at each square?\r\n4. Use Validate to check your work.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from neighborhood import *\n\n# Painter setup: the Painter starts in the top-left corner, facing east.\n# Your code goes below.\n\nmove()\n\nif is_on_bucket():\n    take_paint()\n    take_paint()\n\nmove()\n\nif is_on_bucket():\n    take_paint()\n    take_paint()\n\nmove()\n\nif is_on_bucket():\n    take_paint()\n    take_paint()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": false
        }
